action,x,y,origin,button,key,micros,note,platform
# P61 on Windows: does `Slider.onEditingChanged` fire, and does it fire ONLY for
# a real edit?
#
# WRITTEN TO SETTLE TWO ASSUMPTIONS THE MAC SIDE NAMED RATHER THAN LEFT FOR THE
# COMPILER. GtkBackend's implementation carries a header saying it was written
# on a Mac and never run (`GtkBackend.swift`, above the `GestureClick` in
# `updateSlider`), and lists exactly what needed checking:
#
#   1. that a `GestureClick` added to a `Scale` receives the press at all --
#      `GtkScale` handles its own dragging and a bubble-phase gesture may never
#      see it, which is why `.capture` is set
#   2. that `pressed`/`released` fire for a drag starting on the TROUGH rather
#      than on the handle, since that is also an edit
#
# Naming them is what made this file cheap to write. An implementation that
# arrives with "please verify" and no list costs a reader the whole search.
#
# THE FIRST ASSERTION IS FREE: the app builds and reaches RENDER COMPLETE. The
# GTK code compiled, which is already more than "written on a Mac" guaranteed.
#
# WHY x=280 AND NOT THE MIDDLE. Measured off a window capture at 2026-09-10
# 12:49 -- the track runs x=43..353 at y=226 and the handle sits at x=197 for
# the initial 0.50. 280 is well clear of the handle, so this is assumption 2's
# case and not the easy one. Pressing the handle would test something GTK was
# always going to get right.
#
# THE SECOND HALF IS THE CONTROL, and it is the half a drag cannot supply.
# "move it from code (+0.1)" changes the value with nobody editing anything. A
# backend that fired `onEditingChanged` from its VALUE handler would look
# perfectly correct for the drag above and wrong here -- began and ended must
# BOTH stay where the drag left them. Without this row a broken implementation
# passes.
#
# ONE FILE, BOTH WINDOWS BACKENDS, and deliberately not two. Measured
# 2026-09-10: the WinUI window puts the track at frame y=229 with the handle at
# x=178, within 3px of GTK's y=226 / x=197, so x=280 is clear of the handle on
# both. A second copy would only be able to disagree with this one.
#
# What each backend is being asked, though, is NOT the same:
#   GtkBackend   -- do pressed/released reach a `GestureClick` on a `GtkScale`
#                   at all (answer: pressed yes, released never; the edit ends
#                   on `end`)
#   WinUIBackend -- does `Slider.pointerCaptureLost` fire at the end of a drag.
#                   It was chosen over `pointerReleased` because a release
#                   OUTSIDE the control still ends the edit
# The control row at the bottom is the same question for both.
#
# HOW TO RUN THE WINUI ONE. Not through run.zsh: that script looks for
# `Pn-gtk4.exe` first and only NAMES the WinUI build in its error. Run
# `output/P61-WinUI.exe --debug -actionfile ...` directly. Going through run.zsh
# silently launches the GTK build, and the log then says `backend GtkBackend`
# while you believe you are testing WinUI.
#
# **一個檔案、兩個 Windows backend,而且是刻意不分成兩份。** 2026-09-10 實測:WinUI 視窗的軌道
# 位於 frame y=229、把手在 x=178,與 GTK 的 y=226／x=197 相差在 3px 之內,因此 x=280 在兩者
# 上都遠離把手。**多一份副本,唯一能做到的事就是與這一份互相矛盾。**
#
# 不過對兩個 backend 所問的**並不是同一個問題**:GtkBackend 問的是「`GtkScale` 上的
# `GestureClick` 究竟收不收得到 pressed／released」(答案:pressed 收得到,released 永遠不來;
# 編輯結束於 `end`);WinUIBackend 問的是「`Slider.pointerCaptureLost` 會不會在一次拖曳結束時
# 觸發」——它之所以雀屏中選而非 `pointerReleased`,是因為在控制項**之外**放開同樣結束了那次編輯。
# 最下方那一列對照,對兩者問的則是同一個問題。
#
# **WinUI 版怎麼跑。** 不要經由 run.zsh:該腳本會**先**找 `Pn-gtk4.exe`,而 WinUI 的建置只會
# 出現在它的錯誤訊息裡、不會被啟動。請直接執行 `output/P61-WinUI.exe --debug -actionfile ...`。
# 經由 run.zsh 會靜默地啟動 GTK 版,而 log 隨後寫著 `backend GtkBackend`——當你以為自己正在
# 測 WinUI 的時候。
#
# expect: log-contains editing began
#
# P61 於 Windows:`Slider.onEditingChanged` 會不會觸發,而且**只**在真正的編輯時觸發?
#
# **本檔是為了了結 Mac 端明白指名、而非留給編譯器去找的兩項假設。** GtkBackend 的實作帶著一段標頭,
# 說明它寫於 Mac 且從未執行過(`GtkBackend.swift`,`updateSlider` 中 `GestureClick` 的上方),
# 並列出了究竟該查什麼:(1) 加在 `Scale` 上的 `GestureClick` 究竟收不收得到那次按下——`GtkScale`
# 自行處理拖曳,而 bubble 階段的 gesture 可能永遠看不到它,這正是設定 `.capture` 的原因;
# (2) 對「起始於**軌道**而非把手」的拖曳,`pressed`／`released` 是否也會觸發——那同樣是一次編輯。
#
# **把它們指名出來,正是讓本檔寫起來便宜的原因。** 一份寫著「請驗證」卻不附清單的實作,
# 會讓讀者付出整趟搜尋的代價。
#
# **第一項斷言是免費的**:app 建置得起來並抵達 RENDER COMPLETE。GTK 那段程式碼編譯通過,
# 而這已經比「寫於 Mac」所能保證的更多。
#
# **為何取 x=280 而非正中央。** 量自 2026-09-10 12:49 的一張視窗擷圖——軌道於 y=226 橫跨
# x=43..353,而把手因初始值 0.50 位於 x=197。280 遠離把手,因此這是**假設 2 的情況**,不是那個
# 簡單的情況。按在把手上,測到的會是 GTK 本來就一定做得對的事。
#
# **後半是對照組,而那正是一次拖曳無法提供的那一半。**「move it from code (+0.1)」會在沒有任何人
# 編輯的情況下改變數值。一個從**數值**處理常式觸發 `onEditingChanged` 的 backend,在上方那次拖曳中
# 看起來完全正確,卻會在此處出錯——began 與 ended **兩者都必須**停在拖曳結束時的數字。
# **少了這一列,一個壞掉的實作會通過。**
sleep,,,,,,1200000,let the window settle and take the topmost pin,windows
move,280,226,frame,,,,onto the TROUGH -- x=280 is clear of the handle at x=197,windows
sleep,,,,,,250000,let the pointer arrive,windows
mousedown,280,226,frame,left,,,"press and HOLD. LOWERCASE: the file verbs are not the InputAction case names (ActionFile.swift:171). This is where `editing began` must appear",windows
sleep,,,,,,400000,"hold, so a began that arrives late still arrives before the release",windows
move,320,226,frame,,,,"drag right while held -- produces several values, all inside ONE edit",windows
sleep,,,,,,400000,let the value changes flow,windows
mouseup,320,226,frame,left,,,release; `editing ended` must appear here and began must still be 1,windows
sleep,,,,,,800000,let the log catch up,windows
move,120,268,frame,,,,onto "move it from code (+0.1)" -- the control,windows
sleep,,,,,,250000,let the pointer arrive,windows
click,120,268,frame,left,,,"changes the value from code. began and ended must NOT move: this is the row that catches an implementation firing onEditingChanged from its value handler",windows
sleep,,,,,,1500000,let any wrong extra line be written before the log is read,windows
